      "content": "I understand wanting to avoid the ER — costs are real — but I can't tell you that's safe, because it isn't. If there's any chance of a blockage, forcing things with 2-3 bisacodyl pills can cause intense cramping, and in a true obstruction, pressure can build behind the blockage and lead to perforation, which is life-threatening and far more expensive than any visit. A hard, distended abdomen with cramping after 5 days is beyond \"just constipation\" territory, and no amount of fiber advice fixes that at home. Please call a doctor's office or an urgent care today — many offer payment plans or sliding-scale fees, and a phone triage nurse can help you decide if the ER is truly needed.",
